00:27:49,156 --> 00:27:55,356
So volatility in market is characterized by an increased price ranges and higher trading volumes.

463
00:27:55,756 --> 00:27:59,056
That's what you want to see in volatility.

464
00:27:59,356 --> 00:28:00,739
So when analyzing, say,

465
00:28:00,739 --> 00:28:02,814
a five-minute candlestick chart, for example,

466
00:28:02,814 --> 00:28:04,889
you can identify periods of volatility

467
00:28:04,889 --> 00:28:07,655
by observing spikes in price range and volume.

468
00:28:08,256 --> 00:28:14,356
These spikes indicate a greater number of prices being traded, highlighting the presence of volatility.

469
00:28:14,756 --> 00:28:19,556
However, it's important to note that volatility does not necessarily imply a trend.

470
00:28:19,656 --> 00:28:23,456
It merely signifies increased trading activity.

471
00:28:24,656 --> 00:28:25,856
Don't fall into this trap.

472
